WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.790
In October 2022, prices
were rising at 11.1 per cent

2
00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:06.300
a year in the UK,

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.430
and 10.6 per cent in the euro area.

4
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.380
Energy and food were the
biggest contributors.

5
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:15.000
But this was not one dear product.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.580
Inflation is a rising price level:

7
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.570
prices across the whole economy,

8
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:21.660
climbing year after year.

9
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.730
So what makes prices across a
whole economy keep going up?

10
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.330
In this mission, you'll
shift curves on an AD

11
00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:32.220
and AS diagram and watch
the price level move.

12
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.150
Then you'll use a graph lab:

13
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.140
move two sliders and track the
price level and real output.

14
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.640
Your mission: find out what
really drives prices up

15
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.150
across a whole economy.
